On suitable fixed models, write $C=C_h+C_v$ relative to $U\to T_0$. The divisor $C_h$ is an SNC boundary over the generic point of $T_0$, $C_v\geq-R_s$, and $$\label{num:order-lower}
 P_U(c)\geq K_{\mathcal V_s}+C_h+cM_U.$$ For very general $t$, the same minimum construction for $q_t:W_t\to U_t$, using the adjunction form on $S_t$, gives $C_h|_{U_t}$. In particular, for every rational divisor $Q$ on $U_t$, $$\label{num:fiber-descent}
